{
	"_about": [
		"The public-text rule (CONTRIBUTING.md, \"Commits and pull requests\"): what is never written in the repository, commit messages, branch names or pull request titles and descriptions.",
		"hashed: names kept as the SHA-256 of each lower-case alphanumeric token, so nothing here spells them (other guide products, private material). A phrase matches whole consecutive tokens: the game's \"rested XP\" is two tokens, not a product's name. `node tools/public-text.js --hash <phrase>` prints a phrase's entry.",
		"rules: case-insensitive regular expressions. A \"tree\" rule holds for every tracked file (tests/wording.test.js) and every message; a \"message\" rule only for commit messages, branch names and pull request text, since the words have plain uses in code and data.",
		"match and pass: examples each rule must and must not match (tests/wording.test.js, tests/public-text.test.js). This file is the only one the wording test does not read."
	],
